  "claim": "Mark Ingram Jr. won an award for college football. A player who was born in 1935, defeated the 1990 Tennessee Volunteers football team's head coach for the same award in 1956,",
  "evidencia": "Page: Johnny Majors. Sentence: He finished second to Paul Hornung in voting for the Heisman Trophy in 1956.\nPage: Paul Hornung. Sentence: Paul Vernon Hornung (born December 23, 1935), nicknamed \"The Golden Boy\", is a former professional American football player, a Hall of Fame running back for the Green Bay Packers of the National Football League (NFL) from 1957 to 1966, winning four NFL titles and the first Super Bowl.\nPage: 1990 Tennessee Volunteers football team. Sentence: Playing as a member of the Southeastern Conference (SEC), the team was led by head coach Johnny Majors, in his 14th year, and played their home games at Neyland Stadium in Knoxville, Tennessee.\nPage: Mark Ingram Jr.. Sentence: He played college football for the University of Alabama, won the Heisman Trophy, and was a member of a national championship team.",
