        "original_id": "96c3e030-1b3a-5848-8f5e-b4b4048c09e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johnny Majors, Paul Hornung, Mark Ingram Jr.\n- Organizations: Green Bay Packers, University of Alabama, Tennessee Volunteers, Southeastern Conference, Pro Football Hall of Fame\n- Places: Knoxville, Tennessee, Neyland Stadium\n- Roles: head coach, running back, professional American football player\n- Awards: Heisman Trophy, Super Bowl, NFL titles, national championship\n- Events: 1956 Heisman Trophy voting, 1990 Tennessee Volunteers football season\n\nFacts:\n- In 1956, Johnny Majors finished second to Paul Hornung in voting for the Heisman Trophy.\n- Paul Hornung was born on December 23, 1935.\n- From 1957 to 1966, Paul Hornung played professional American football as a running back for the Green Bay Packers in the National Football League.\n- Paul Hornung won four NFL titles and the first Super Bowl with the Green Bay Packers.\n- Paul Hornung is a Pro Football Hall of Fame running back and was nicknamed \"The Golden Boy.\"\n- In 1990, Johnny Majors was the head coach of the Tennessee Volunteers football team in his 14th year.\n- In 1990, the Tennessee Volunteers football team competed in the Southeastern Conference and played home games at Neyland Stadium in Knoxville, Tennessee.\n- Mark Ingram Jr. played college football for the University of Alabama.\n- Mark Ingram Jr. won the Heisman Trophy and was a member of a national championship team.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
